		{
			"id": "eOlmjVdw2seLCdixz",
			"description": "Equalisers (pair)",
			"local_notes": "A matched pair: wield one in each hand with the Dual-Weapon Attack technique (B230) or fight with one and parry with the other. Each blade parries separately (Parry 0 on Shortsword). Mundane: no armour divisor.\n\nLore: Paired Ethereal blades: the framework's brief lists equalisers as Ethereal fighting swords in pairs. I hold the name and the paired form with low confidence and have no source for lengths or weights, so this entry is deliberately plain.\n\nDesign: A pair of light one-handed blades of the Shortsword family (Basic Set: sw cut, thr imp), given the modest +1 of a good weapon. At an Ethereal's ST 9: swing 1d cut (average 3.5, x1.5 wounding), which goes through flak 0.0% of the time and nothing armoured. Weight 3 lb the pair (1.5 lb each), Min ST 8 (a set at ST 9 hands is a light load, and a ritual pair has some length; the pure weight rule sqrt(10x1.5)=3.9 would allow less, so 8 is a design floor). TL 8 and cost $2,400 for the pair, as for the honour blade. Dual-Weapon Attack is the Basic Set technique for two blades.",
